<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 180 0 R
/T (The Black Women's March for Reparations and Well-living \(buen vivir\) is a nationwide mobilization that brings together Black women from across Brazil in the fight against racism, sexism, and other structural inequalities that intersect and shape our lives and territories. In 2025, we return to the streets with another central and urgent demand: Reproductive Justice, an expression of the autonomy, self-determination, and dignity in our sexual and reproductive lives that we have been claiming for centuries.)
/E (The Black Women's March for Reparations and Well-living \(buen vivir\) is a nationwide mobilization that brings together Black women from across Brazil in the fight against racism, sexism, and other structural inequalities that intersect and shape our lives and territories. In 2025, we return to the streets with another central and urgent demand: Reproductive Justice, an expression of the autonomy, self-determination, and dignity in our sexual and reproductive lives that we have been claiming for centuries.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
