311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 180 0 R
/T (More than the right to choose, Reproductive Justice affirms that reproductive freedom is only possible when the conditions for a life of dignity are fully realized. In this sense, Reproductive Justice is inseparable from Social Justice. This framework encompasses all people affected by reproductive inequities, including Black women, people who can become pregnant, trans men, travestis, people with disabilities, and people living with HIV/AIDS.)
/E (More than the right to choose, Reproductive Justice affirms that reproductive freedom is only possible when the conditions for a life of dignity are fully realized. In this sense, Reproductive Justice is inseparable from Social Justice. This framework encompasses all people affected by reproductive inequities, including Black women, people who can become pregnant, trans men, travestis, people with disabilities, and people living with HIV/AIDS.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
