351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Institutional racism lies at the heart of health inequities. It is inscribed on the bodies of Black women and all people who can become pregnant. It manifests in denied access to care, in pain that is dismissed, and in preventable deaths. The findings from the mapping process point to a system that determines who is allowed to live with dignity and who is left to fend for themselves. When the State denies care, it reinforces the racial pact that sustains exclusion. Confronting institutional racism is essential to the full realization of Reproductive Justice.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
