/P 203 0 R
/E (The testimonies revealed experiences of obstetric violence, medical neglect, and medical racism, as well as racism perpetrated by other healthcare professionals. The absence of memory enables these harms to persist: our bodies carry the histories of violence that the State seeks to erase. Reproductive justice requires both material and symbolic reparations, as well as a commitment to ensuring that such abuses are never repeated. Memory is a future-making policy.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
